# Theorem 1: Modus Ponens
# P→Q, P ⊢ Q
0 ~P Q
1 P
2 ~Q
3 Q from 0 1
4 from 3 2

# Theorem 2: Modus Tollens
# P→Q, ¬Q ⊢ ¬P
0 ~P Q
1 ~Q
2 P
3 ~P from 0 1
4 from 2 3

# Theorem 3: Hypothetical Syllogism
# P→Q, Q→R, P, ¬R ⊢ □
0 ~P(X) Q(X)
1 ~Q(Y) R(Y)
2 P(a)
3 ~R(a)
4 Q(a) from 0 2
5 R(a) from 1 4
6 from 5 3

# Theorem 4: Disjunctive Syllogism
# P∨Q, ¬P, ¬Q ⊢ □
0 P Q
1 ~P
2 ~Q
3 Q from 0 1
4 from 3 2

# Theorem 5: Constructive Dilemma
# (P→Q)∧(R→S)∧P∧R∧¬Q ⊢ □
0 ~P Q
1 ~R S
2 P
3 R
4 ~Q
5 Q from 0 2
6 from 5 4

